{
  "conformance": "enrich.lead-scored",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "status": "ruled",
  "basis": [
    "the score fact's producer invariants, which its published schema cannot state",
    "the composite's arithmetic: contributions summed in double precision in the rubric's declared order, rounded once, half-to-even, to 4 places, and banded on the rounded value"
  ],
  "rule": "Two kinds of vector. An input with score is a lead.scored.v1 payload; expect is holds, or the first rule it breaks, in the order schema, no_null, no_empty_string, non_negative, outcome_fields, grades. schema: typeRef.version is an integer, the one typed field these vectors check. no_null: no value is null. no_empty_string: no present string is empty. non_negative: ceiling is at least 0 and composite, a decimal string of scale 4, is at least 0.0000. outcome_fields: scored has a band and no disqualifier; disqualified has no band, composite 0.0000 and a disqualifier; operatorCompletion is present exactly when scoredBy is operator_completed. grades: each criterion is graded at most once and is not also pending an operator; confidence is within 0.0000 to 1.0000, present on every engine grade and absent on every operator grade. An input with composition is the arithmetic: composite is the sum of grade times weight over the accepted grades, in the criteria's declared order, in IEEE-754 double precision, rounded once half-to-even on the double's exact binary value to 4 places; band is the first band in declared order whose threshold the rounded composite is at least. The weights and thresholds in these vectors are synthetic.",
